    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey im having a bit of a headache with aws. i'm trying to get a lambda function to write logs to an s3 bucket but i keep getting an Access Denied error in the cloudwatch logs even though i thought i set the permissions up right. \n\nhere is the iam policy i attached to the lambda role:\n\n{\n  \"Version\": \"2012-10-17\",\n  \"Statement\": [\n    {\n      \"Effect\": \"Allow\",\n      \"Action\": [\n        \"s3:PutObject\"\n      ],\n      \"Resource\": \"arn:aws:s3:::my-app-logs-bucket\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n\ncan u take a look and tell me whats wrong?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The issue might not be directly related to the IAM policy, but rather the permissions that the IAM role itself has, especially theapphire IAM role trust relationships. Can you please check the AWS IAM role trust relationship to see if it includes permissions to cloudwatch for writing logs to S3? Also, ensure that you have an `S3BucketPolicy` that grants the necessary permissions to upload logs to your S3 bucket.",
      "source": "target",
