      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "`s3:PutObject Receipt` is indeed a real permission, but it's not the primary cause of the issue. \n\nAnother possible cause is that Elastic load balancer, Application Load Balancer, or CloudFront entries might be altering the request headers, which can lead to issues with CloudWatch logging. Also, make sure that your Lambda function is being authenticated by AWS IAM correctly. Check the X-Amz-I (ID) header in the CloudWatch logs to ensure that it matches the IAM role's Amazon Resource Name (ARN).",
